<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fort Rosalie</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1716">1716</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fort Rosalie was a French fort built in 1716 on the bluffs of the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi River</a> at present-day Natchez, Mississippi, in the colony of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana">Louisiana</a>. A French settlement and tobacco plantations grew around it on Natchez land. In November 1729 the Natchez rose and killed most of the French settlers there, and French reprisals over the following years destroyed the Natchez as an independent people.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fort-rosalie.jpg" alt="Fort Rosalie" width="320" height="229" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Collot, Georges Henri Victor · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:View_of_the_Fort_of_the_Natchez.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
